## Page Object Model Conventions

Every Page Object must follow this exact pattern:

```typescript
import { Page, Locator, expect } from '@playwright/test';

export class [PageName]Page {
  readonly page: Page;

  // Locators — all defined in constructor, never inline
  readonly [elementName]: Locator;

  constructor(page: Page) {
    this.page = page;
    this.[elementName] = page.getByRole('[role]', { name: '[name]' });
  }

  // Navigation
  async goto() {
    await this.page.goto('/[path]');
  }

  // Actions — one action per method, named as verbs
  async [actionName]([params]: [type]) {
    await this.[elementName].[action]([params]);
  }

  // Assertions — prefixed with "expect"
  async expect[StateName]() {
    await expect(this.[elementName]).toBeVisible();
  }
}
```

**Rules:**
- Always import `expect` from `@playwright/test` in Page Objects
- All locators defined in the constructor, never inline in methods
- Prefer `getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByPlaceholder` over CSS selectors
- Never use `page.$()` or `page.$$()` — always use Playwright's recommended locators
- Action methods named as verbs: `clickLogin()`, `fillEmail()`, `selectOption()`
- Assertion methods prefixed with `expect`: `expectErrorVisible()`, `expectDashboardLoaded()`
- One responsibility per method — never combine actions

