## Spec File Conventions

Every spec file must follow this exact pattern. Use Autoframe's custom fixtures (not raw `page`) when a fixture is available for the Page Object being tested:

```typescript
import { test, expect } from '../../../fixtures/[feature]Fixtures';
import { [PageName]Page } from '../../../pages/[feature-name]/[PageName]Page';

test.describe('[Feature Name]', () => {

  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    // setup — navigate to starting URL or reset state
  });

  test.afterEach(async ({ page }) => {
    // cleanup if needed
  });

  test.describe('Happy Path', () => {
    test('[user story in plain language]', async ({ [pageName]Page }) => {
      // Arrange
      // (data setup if needed)

      // Act
      await [pageName]Page.[action]();

      // Assert
      await [pageName]Page.expect[State]();
    });
  });

  test.describe('Negative Cases', () => {
    test('[negative scenario in plain language]', async ({ [pageName]Page }) => {
      // Arrange
      // Act
      // Assert
    });
  });

  test.describe('Edge Cases', () => {
    test('[edge scenario in plain language]', async ({ [pageName]Page }) => {
      // Arrange
      // Act
      // Assert
    });
  });

});
```

**When no fixture exists yet for the Page Object**, use raw `page` as a fallback and add a comment:

```typescript
// TODO: create fixture for [PageName]Page
test('[scenario]', async ({ page }) => {
  const [pageName]Page = new [PageName]Page(page);
  // ...
});
```

**Rules:**
- Always use Arrange / Act / Assert comments inside each test
- Always group tests: Happy Path, Negative Cases, Edge Cases
- If Negative/Edge cases need different setup than the Happy Path (e.g. an unauthenticated-access test must skip login), move `beforeEach` into the inner `describe` blocks instead of the top level
- Test names must be written in plain language a non-technical person can read
- Never put logic inside `test.describe` blocks, only inside `test` blocks
- Prefer custom fixtures over raw `page` whenever a fixture exists
- Always import from Autoframe fixtures, not directly from `@playwright/test` when fixtures are available

