## API Test Conventions

Every API test file must follow this pattern:

```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe('[Endpoint] API', () => {

  test('GET [endpoint] returns [expected]', async ({ request }) => {
    const response = await request.get('/api/[endpoint]', {
      headers: {
        'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.API_TOKEN}`
      }
    });

    expect(response.status()).toBe(200);
    const body = await response.json();
    expect(body).toMatchObject({
      // schema validation
    });
  });

  test('GET [endpoint] returns 401 when unauthenticated', async ({ request }) => {
    const response = await request.get('/api/[endpoint]');
    expect(response.status()).toBe(401);
  });

  test('POST [endpoint] returns 400 for invalid input', async ({ request }) => {
    const response = await request.post('/api/[endpoint]', {
      data: { /* invalid payload */ }
    });
    expect(response.status()).toBe(400);
  });

});
```

**Rules:**
- Always validate response status code
- Always validate response schema with `toMatchObject`
- Always use environment variables for auth tokens, never hardcode
- Always cover: success response, error response, auth failure, invalid input
- API test files use kebab-case + `.api.spec.ts` suffix: `auth.api.spec.ts`

